{"name":"Reflection","hex":"#d3d5d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"reflection","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of reflecting or the state of being reflected.","The property of a propagated wave being thrown back from a surface (such as a mirror)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflection"}],"entries":[{"title":"Reflection (physics)","blocks":[{"text":"Reflection is the change in direction of a wavefront at an interface between two different media so that the wavefront returns into the medium from which it originated. Common examples include the reflection of light, sound and water waves. The law of reflection says that for specular reflection the angle at which the wave is incident on the surface equals the angle at which it is reflected."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mount_Hood_reflected_in_Mirror_Lake%2C_Oregon.jpg/330px-Mount_Hood_reflected_in_Mirror_Lake%2C_Oregon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reflection_(physics)"},{"title":"Specular reflection","blocks":[{"text":"Specular reflection, or regular reflection, is the mirror-like reflection of waves, such as light, from a surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Reflection_angles.svg/330px-Reflection_angles.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Specular_reflection"},{"title":"Reflection (C++)","blocks":[{"text":"Reflection in C++ refers to the usage of reflective programming, introduced to the C++ programming language in C++26. Reflection in C++, unlike other languages like Java and C#, occurs at compile time and incurs no runtime overhead."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reflection_(C%2B%2B)"},{"title":"Reflection (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Reflection\" is a song written and produced by Matthew Wilder and David Zippel for the soundtrack of Disney's 1998 animated film Mulan. In the film, the song is performed by Tony Award winner, Filipina singer and actress Lea Salonga as the film's titular character. \"Reflection\" has received highly positive reviews, with critics highlighting its emotional writing and Salonga's vocals. Despite not being released as a single, nor making any chart, the song would later be certified 2× Platinum by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA) for equivalent sales of 2,000,000 units in the United States, and was certified Silver by the British Phonographic Industry (BPI) for equivalent sales of 200,000 units in the United Kingdom. An accompanying music video for \"Reflection\" was included as a bonus to the Disney Gold Classic Collection DVD release of the film in February 2000."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reflection_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/MIT_4.492_Daylighting%2C_Fall_2004_-_Types_of_Reflection_-_4815499473.jpg/500px-MIT_4.492_Daylighting%2C_Fall_2004_-_Types_of_Reflection_-_4815499473.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/MIT_4.492_Daylighting%2C_Fall_2004_-_Types_of_Reflection_-_4815499473.jpg/500px-MIT_4.492_Daylighting%2C_Fall_2004_-_Types_of_Reflection_-_4815499473.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sketches of specular, spread, diffuse, and compound reflection.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMIT_4.492_Daylighting%2C_Fall_2004_-_Types_of_Reflection_-_4815499473.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/F%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg/500px-F%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/F%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg/1280px-F%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/F%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg/500px-F%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example of the law of reflection","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AF%C3%A9nyvisszaver%C5%91d%C3%A9s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Studio_soundproofing_panel.jpg/500px-Studio_soundproofing_panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Studio_soundproofing_panel.jpg/1280px-Studio_soundproofing_panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Studio_soundproofing_panel.jpg/500px-Studio_soundproofing_panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sound diffusion panel for high frequencies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStudio_soundproofing_panel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg/500px-Tso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg/1280px-Tso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg/500px-Tso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reflections on still water are an example of specular reflection.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATso_Kiagar_Lake_Ladakh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/